{% comment %}
  "WHY YOU'LL LOVE IT" - a small uppercase label, one serif line, and a stack
  of icon + heading + body rows on a sand card, closed by a full-bleed image.

  The copy is per product and comes from metafields; the icons are per template
  and come from block settings. Which metafield a row reads is decided by its
  position, so the first block reads custom.usp_1_heading / custom.usp_1_text,
  the second reads usp_2_*, and so on up to usp_6_*. Reordering the blocks in
  the theme editor reorders which metafield shows where, which is the behaviour
  a merchant dragging a row expects.

  Each row falls back to text typed on its own block when the metafield is
  empty, so the section is visible and editable before any metafield exists.
  Filling the metafield on a product overrides the fallback for that product
  only - which is the point: the fallback is the collection-level claim, the
  metafield is the one true of this specific garment.

  A row with neither is skipped, and the section renders nothing at all when
  no row survives, so clearing all the fallbacks is how you turn it off.

  One row can be marked "Highlight", which inverts it to the brand green and
  bleeds it to the card's edges - the design uses it for "Made in small
  batches", which used to be a full-width band of its own. Marking two rows
  works, but the design intends one.

  Metafields read:
  - custom.usp_1_heading .. custom.usp_6_heading  (single line text)
  - custom.usp_1_text    .. custom.usp_6_text     (multi-line text)
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'product-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign rendered = 0
  assign headings = ''
  assign bodies = ''
  assign icons = ''
  assign highlights = ''

  for block in section.blocks
    assign heading_key = 'usp_' | append: forloop.index | append: '_heading'
    assign text_key = 'usp_' | append: forloop.index | append: '_text'

    assign heading = product.metafields.custom[heading_key].value | default: product.metafields.custom[heading_key]
    assign body = product.metafields.custom[text_key].value | default: product.metafields.custom[text_key]

    comment
      Fall back per field rather than per row: a product that has a heading
      metafield but no body should keep the block's body, not lose it.
    endcomment
    if heading == blank
      assign heading = block.settings.heading
    endif
    if body == blank
      assign body = block.settings.text
    endif

    if heading != blank
      assign rendered = rendered | plus: 1
      assign headings = headings | append: heading | append: '~|~'
      assign bodies = bodies | append: body | append: '~|~'
      assign icons = icons | append: block.settings.icon | append: '~|~'
      comment
        Flags carry a value for every surviving row so this list stays the same
        length as the other three and can be read by the same index. A bare
        boolean appended to a string is '' when false, which would collapse two
        entries into one.
      endcomment
      if block.settings.highlight
        assign highlights = highlights | append: '1' | append: '~|~'
      else
        assign highlights = highlights | append: '0' | append: '~|~'
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign heading_list = headings | split: '~|~'
  assign body_list = bodies | split: '~|~'
  assign icon_list = icons | split: '~|~'
  assign highlight_list = highlights | split: '~|~'
-%}

{%- if rendered > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="pdp-section pdp-why color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient"
    style="--pdp-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --pdp-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;"
  >
    <div class="pdp-section__inner">
      {%- comment -%}
        `--split` rather than `:has(.pdp-why__media)`, so the two-column rule
        keys off something Liquid knows for certain. Without an image there is
        no second column to fill, and a card that went to two columns anyway
        would put half a page of empty sand beside the rows.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          One "is there media" answer for the class, the ratio and the render,
          rather than three conditions that can disagree. A Shopify-hosted video
          wins over an external URL, and either wins over the image - so a
          merchant who adds a video to a card that already had a photo gets the
          video, and can go back by clearing it.
        endcomment
        assign has_video = false
        if section.settings.video != blank or section.settings.video_url != blank
          assign has_video = true
        endif
        assign has_media = false
        if has_video or section.settings.image != blank
          assign has_media = true
        endif

        assign split = '1fr 1fr'
        if section.settings.desktop_split == 'copy'
          assign split = '1.25fr 0.75fr'
        elsif section.settings.desktop_split == 'media'
          assign split = '0.75fr 1.25fr'
        endif
      -%}
      <div
        class="pdp-why__card{% if has_media %} pdp-why__card--split{% endif %}{% if section.settings.mobile_media_first %} pdp-why__card--media-first{% endif %}"
        style="--pdp-why-split: {{ split }};{% if section.settings.media_ratio != 'adapt' %} --pdp-why-ratio: {{ section.settings.media_ratio }};{% endif %}"
      >
        <div class="pdp-why__content">
          {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp-eyebrow pdp-why__label">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp-why__lede">{{ section.settings.lede | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <ul class="pdp-why__list">
            {%- for heading in heading_list -%}
              {%- assign is_highlight = false -%}
              {%- if highlight_list[forloop.index0] == '1' -%}
                {%- assign is_highlight = true -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              <li class="pdp-why__row{% if is_highlight %} pdp-why__row--highlight{% endif %}">
                {%- assign icon_name = icon_list[forloop.index0] -%}
                {%- if icon_name != blank and icon_name != 'none' -%}
                  <span class="pdp-why__icon">
                    {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: icon_name -%}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="pdp-why__body">
                  <h3 class="pdp-why__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h3>
                  {%- assign body = body_list[forloop.index0] -%}
                  {%- if body != blank -%}
                    <p class="pdp-why__text">{{ body | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The media. Outside .pdp-why__content, so it reaches the card's edges
          without cancelling the content's padding: from 990px it is the card's
          second column, below that it stacks - above the rows by default,
          because that is where the reviewed mobile design puts it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_media -%}
          <div class="pdp-why__media{% if has_video %} pdp-why__media--video{% endif %}{% if section.settings.media_ratio != 'adapt' %} pdp-why__media--ratio{% endif %}">
            {%- if section.settings.video != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A Shopify-hosted video, so autoplay, muting and looping are
                attributes on a real <video> rather than provider query
                parameters. `muted` is forced on whenever autoplay is on: every
                browser blocks an unmuted autoplay, and the failure is silent -
                a poster frame that never moves and no error anywhere.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign v_muted = section.settings.video_mute
                if section.settings.video_autoplay
                  assign v_muted = true
                endif
              -%}
              {{
                section.settings.video
                | video_tag:
                  image_size: '1400x',
                  autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                  loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                  muted: v_muted,
                  controls: section.settings.video_controls,
                  preload: 'metadata'
              }}
            {%- elsif section.settings.video_url != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                YouTube and Vimeo do not take the same parameters: YouTube wants
                `mute` and needs `playlist` set to its own id before `loop` does
                anything at all, Vimeo wants `muted`. Sending one provider the
                other's names is accepted and ignored, which looks like the
                setting simply not working.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="pdp-why__embed">
                {%- if section.settings.video_url.type == 'youtube' -%}
                  {{
                    section.settings.video_url
                    | external_video_url:
                      autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      mute: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                      playlist: section.settings.video_url.id,
                      controls: section.settings.video_controls
                    | external_video_tag: loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{
                    section.settings.video_url
                    | external_video_url:
                      autoplay: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      muted: section.settings.video_autoplay,
                      loop: section.settings.video_loop,
                      controls: section.settings.video_controls
                    | external_video_tag: loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- else -%}
              {{
                section.settings.image
                | image_url: width: 1400
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw',
                  widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1400',
                  alt: section.settings.image.alt
              }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP: Why you'll love it",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "pdp-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each row shows the product metafield when it is set — custom.usp_1_heading and custom.usp_1_text for row one, usp_2_* for row two, and so on — and the text typed on the block otherwise. Clear both and that row is hidden."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Section label",
      "default": "Why you'll love it",
      "info": "The small uppercase line above the card."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lede",
      "label": "Opening line",
      "default": "Clothes with character, made for comfort.",
      "info": "One serif line under the label. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Closing image",
      "info": "Sits at the foot of the card, full width. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A video wins over the image when one is set, and a Shopify-hosted video wins over a URL. Clear the video to go back to the photo."
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "Video (uploaded)"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "Video link",
      "accept": [
        "youtube",
        "vimeo"
      ],
      "info": "Used only when no uploaded video is set."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_autoplay",
      "label": "Autoplay",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Muting is forced on while autoplay is on — browsers block an unmuted autoplay silently."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_mute",
      "label": "Mute",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_loop",
      "label": "Loop",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_controls",
      "label": "Show player controls",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "Media shape",
      "default": "adapt",
      "info": "Applies where the media stacks under 990px. From 990px it is one half of the card and fills that column's height.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "adapt",
          "label": "Adapt to the media"
        },
        {
          "value": "1 / 1",
          "label": "Square (1:1)"
        },
        {
          "value": "4 / 5",
          "label": "Portrait (4:5)"
        },
        {
          "value": "3 / 4",
          "label": "Portrait (3:4)"
        },
        {
          "value": "4 / 3",
          "label": "Landscape (4:3)"
        },
        {
          "value": "3 / 2",
          "label": "Landscape (3:2)"
        },
        {
          "value": "16 / 9",
          "label": "Wide (16:9)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "desktop_split",
      "label": "Desktop split",
      "default": "even",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "even",
          "label": "Even halves"
        },
        {
          "value": "copy",
          "label": "Wider copy"
        },
        {
          "value": "media",
          "label": "Wider media"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "mobile_media_first",
      "label": "Show media first on mobile",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colors.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.padding.section_padding_heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "column",
      "name": "Row",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "default": "leaf",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "none",
              "label": "None"
            },
            {
              "value": "leaf",
              "label": "Leaf"
            },
            {
              "value": "flower",
              "label": "Flower"
            },
            {
              "value": "needle",
              "label": "Needle and thread"
            },
            {
              "value": "shield",
              "label": "Shield"
            },
            {
              "value": "box",
              "label": "Parcel"
            },
            {
              "value": "feather",
              "label": "Feather"
            },
            {
              "value": "hand",
              "label": "Hand"
            },
            {
              "value": "weave",
              "label": "Weave"
            },
            {
              "value": "block-print",
              "label": "Block print"
            },
            {
              "value": "garment",
              "label": "Garment"
            },
            {
              "value": "tag",
              "label": "Tag"
            },
            {
              "value": "exchange",
              "label": "Exchange"
            },
            {
              "value": "process",
              "label": "Process"
            },
            {
              "value": "person",
              "label": "Person"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "info": "Used when this row's metafield is empty."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "info": "Used when this row's metafield is empty."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "highlight",
          "label": "Highlight this row",
          "default": false,
          "info": "Inverts the row to the brand green and bleeds it to the card's edges. The design uses this on one row only."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "PDP: Why you'll love it",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "leaf"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "flower"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "needle"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shield"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "box",
            "highlight": true
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
